id: ops-0u7l
title: Characterize pre-existing fleet workflow scanner refusals
description: "The canonical auditor already refuses conditional regex operands in pm-changelog/release.yml and pm-github/pm-github-sync.yml, plus non-shell or unresolved content in four core workflows. The #148/#149 compatibility inventory found no newly failing previously passing workflows. Preserve fail-closed behavior while adding narrow positive and negative controls for any future scanner support."
type: Task
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-13T13:18:34.238Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-15T20:39:09.127Z"
author: codex-sol
comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-13T14:42:42.892Z",pi-agent,"Fleet inventory reproduced on the candidate source: 112 workflow files, 22 PASS (identical to baseline), 84 NO_PUBLISH, 6 pre-existing FAILs (pm-changelog/release.yml, pm-github/pm-github-sync.yml, and four pm-cli workflows). The new YAML-based auditor additionally resolves three baseline refusals (pm-rust/release.yml, pm-cli/ci.yml, pm-cli/codeql.yml) to NO_PUBLISH without any false acceptance. Follow-up remains for a future owner; no change needed by this PR."
  "2026-10-13T22:23:25.464Z",claude-hub,"Reopened: this item was linked in the merged PR body as an open follow-up or risk, not as delivered work. The automated close-out closed it in error; it remains open."
  "2026-10-15T20:04:34.489Z",codex-agent,"Reusing the existing fleet scanner-refusal item for issue #172. Baseline origin/main is 84221c8 (includes #171). Implement word contexts for Bash conditional operands and compound array assignments, retaining executable substitution scans and fail-closed incomplete input. Verify exact fleet constructs with inert Bash publishers, paired adversarial tests, per-change behavioral reverts, read-only built fleet comparison, and unchanged npm/Bun release gates. Other existing fleet non-passes remain out of scope."
  "2026-10-15T20:09:27.022Z",codex-agent,"Focused Bash-backed regression suite: 38/38 pass directly and through pm test --run --progress, covering exact issue lines in shell and YAML bodies, literal regex syntax, array assignment/append, executable substitutions, same-line commands, and incomplete contexts. pm test reports evidence_recording.recorded=false (tracking_disabled); results are recorded here. Built fleet comparison fixes pm-changelog; pm-github still has eight older variable-expanded case-arm refusals in the sync workflow. All other fleet verdicts are unchanged, including the expected pm-cli and pm-rust non-passes. Investigating that additional acceptance blocker separately from the requested operand changes."
  "2026-10-15T20:15:11.716Z",codex-agent,"Built verifier fleet proof: imported dist/attestation.js, ran verify(root), and called report(result, write, exit) on every fleet checkout containing .github/workflows/release.yml. Same source checkouts were read only. Counts in parentheses are refusals. pm-changelog and pm-github now PASS. Every other verdict is unchanged; pm-cli and pm-rust remain expected non-passes and out of scope. pm-github also required word handling for its older variable-expanded case-arm patterns; the focused suite now includes paired Bash controls for those patterns, nested bodies, substitutions and fallthrough.\n\n| Checkout | Main 84221c8 | Candidate |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| pm-ado | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-beads | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-brief | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-changelog | FAIL (1) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-cli | FAIL (48) | FAIL (45) |\n| pm-context | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-csv | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-gantt-chart | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-github | FAIL (15) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-graph | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-jev | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-jira | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-linear | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-lint | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-ops | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-presets | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-review | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-rl | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-rust | FAIL (1) | FAIL (1) |\n| pm-slack | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-slack-standup | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-starter | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-swarm | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-todos | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-ts-starter | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-vcs | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |\n| pm-web | PASS (0) | PASS (0) |"
  "2026-10-15T20:16:21.331Z",codex-agent,"Design acceptance: retain existing conditional token contract, suppress shell-command boundaries only in conditional words and array assignment elements, and recurse into genuine substitutions. The full pm-github PASS requirement additionally needs a case-state stack to distinguish pattern words from arm commands. Function-only behavioral proof against 84221c8: scanner reverted gives 0/2 pass for exact version-regex fixtures, 0/1 for the exact quoted array, and 0/2 for variable case patterns; command-prefix function reverted independently gives 0/1 for array append with unresolved elements. These are assertion failures, with no loader/syntax errors. Restored candidate passes all three exact fleet fixtures. Proof ran in an isolated copy so concurrent gate sources stayed intact."
  "2026-10-15T20:39:05.086Z",codex-agent,"Gates: `npm run release:check` with a fresh HOME and no global/system Git config, and `bun run release:check`, both passed at unchanged thresholds. Each: 1,287 tests, 1,285 passed, 0 failed/cancelled/todo, 2 optional live-repository skips; 100% statements/branches/functions/lines across all 25 measured source files. Duplication 0% across 69 sources; 242 declarations documented; production audit 0 vulnerabilities. The skipped optional fleet CLI tests do not supply live acceptance evidence; the requested built-verifier fleet proof was run independently. Focused Bash controls: node --test test/regex-array.test.ts, 63/63; broader focused scanner suites, 249/249. All code, tests and generated output were unchanged between the final gates. pm test --run --progress passed the linked 63 tests; project policy disables automatic test-result storage, so manual comments retain the result. No new pm CLI defect was found. Item remains in_progress for orchestrator verification; claim is released at handoff."
